{number: 124}
{title: The First Noel}
{key: D}

{start_of_verse: 1}
The [D] first No-[A] el the [G] angel did [D] say
Was to [G] certain poor [D] shepherds in [G] fields as they [D] lay;
In [D] fields where [A] they lay [G] keeping their [D] sheep,
On a [G] cold winter's [D] night that [G] was so [D] deep.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
No-[D] el, No-[F#m] el, No-[G] el, No-[D] el,
[G] Born is the [D] King of [G] Is-[A7] ra-[D] el.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
They [D] looked [A] up and [G] saw a [D] star
Shining [G] in the [D] east, be-[G] yond them [D] far;
And [D] to the [A] earth it [G] gave great [D] light,
And [G] so it con-[D] tinued both [G] day and [D] night.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
And [D] by the [A] light of [G] that same [D] star
Three [G] Wise Men [D] came from [G] country [D] far;
To [D] seek for a [A] king was [G] their in-[D] tent,
And to [G] follow the [D] star wher-[G] ever it [D] went.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
Then [D] let us [A] all with [G] one ac-[D] cord
Sing [G] praises [D] to our [G] heav'nly [D] Lord;
That [D] hath made [A] heav'n and [G] earth of [D] naught,
And [G] with His [D] blood man-[G] kind hath [D] bought.
{end_of_verse}
